# 19. Troubleshooting

## Problem 1: Docker command not found

Run:

```bash
docker --version
```

If it isn't recognized, install Docker Desktop and restart the terminal.

---

## Problem 2: Docker Desktop isn't running

Start Docker Desktop and wait until Docker reports that it is running.

Then:

```bash
docker ps
```

---

## Problem 3: Port 8080 already in use

This is common if Jenkins is already running on port 8080.

Use another host port, for example **8081**:

```bash
docker run -d -p 8081:80 --name docker-web-container docker-web-app
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:8081
```

Remember:

```text
8081:80
│    │
│    └── Docker container port
└─────── Computer/host port
```

---

## Problem 4: Container name already exists

You may get:

```text
Conflict. The container name is already in use.
```

Check:

```bash
docker ps -a
```

Remove the old container:

```bash
docker rm -f docker-web-container
```

Then run:

```bash
docker run -d -p 8080:80 --name docker-web-container docker-web-app
```

